1
00:01:36,130 --> 00:01:40,050
[River of No Return]

2
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:43,030
[Episode 9: Letter of Passage]

3
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,440
I understand, Your Majesty.

4
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:48,550
Please say no more, Your Majesty.

5
00:01:49,550 --> 00:01:50,800
I understand.

6
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:52,860
Your Highness the Prince of Han,

7
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:55,210
I've already told my wife that you like

8
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:57,100
osmanthus rice cakes.

9
00:01:57,330 --> 00:01:59,990
We'll send you some more
when we have the chance.

10
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,930
Your Excellencies, please get up.

11
00:02:05,890 --> 00:02:06,690
Please get up.

12
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:08,979
Hurry up and get up.

13
00:02:08,979 --> 00:02:10,039
Didn't you hear me?

14
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:11,710
Hurry up and get up.

15
00:02:17,329 --> 00:02:20,030
By His Majesty's oral decree:

16
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:23,030
Thanks to your sincere prayers,

17
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:25,430
my condition is now stable.

18
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:26,980
I think of

19
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:29,870
how you've attended to me
for days without rest,

20
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:31,520
unable to sleep or eat in peace,

21
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:33,300
and I can bear to see it no longer.

22
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:34,760
Therefore, I hereby grant

23
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,050
all attending officials permission

24
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:38,910
to temporarily return
to their residences to rest.

25
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:42,520
We humbly obey Your Majesty's decree.

26
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:44,640
Alright, Your Excellencies, hurry home.

27
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:45,650
Hurry and gather your belongings.

28
00:02:45,650 --> 00:02:47,180
Thank you for your efforts.

29
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:50,430
Your Highness the Prince of Han,

30
00:02:50,430 --> 00:02:51,390
please go home.

31
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:54,930
Is that true?

32
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:56,400
Yes.

33
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,220
Please go home.

34
00:02:59,360 --> 00:02:59,960
Lord Lyu,

35
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:02,380
gather your things and head home.

36
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:04,200
Lord Liu, you've worked hard.

37
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,140
Thank you for your efforts,
Your Excellencies.

38
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,800
Stop chatting and hurry home.

39
00:03:07,990 --> 00:03:08,770
Hurry home,

40
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,970
Your Excellencies.

41
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:16,700
Hurry up and pack.

42
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:17,590
Take it away.

43
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:24,480
Your Highness.

44
00:03:26,829 --> 00:03:28,630
Your Highness the Prince of Han?

45
00:03:28,890 --> 00:03:29,690
The people from your residence

46
00:03:29,690 --> 00:03:31,220
are here to escort you home.

47
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:33,390
This servant will see you out now?

48
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:47,060
[Zhu Zhanyu,
Fifth Son of the Prince of Han]

49
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:42,800
Father.

50
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:45,320
In a few more days,

51
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,850
you won't have to
wear this blue robe anymore.

52
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:49,480
The color of the dragon throne

53
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,030
suits you far better.

54
00:03:51,610 --> 00:03:54,180
Right now, the Emperor is getting better,

55
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:55,940
and the Crown Prince is missing.

56
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:56,960
It's

57
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:59,460
too early to say.

58
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:03,830
The last time I came here

59
00:04:03,830 --> 00:04:06,630
was 10 years ago,
when Grandfather issued an edict

60
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:10,490
praising Imperial Grandson Zhu Zhanji for
his service against the Oirat and summoned

61
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:15,020
all his grandsons to the Hall of Literary Brilliance
to pay their respects to him.

62
00:04:16,149 --> 00:04:17,390
That very day,

63
00:04:18,550 --> 00:04:20,529
I finally saw clearly

64
00:04:20,550 --> 00:04:22,380
what kind of man my cousin truly was.

65
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,040
The Crown Prince has arrived!

66
00:04:33,650 --> 00:04:34,770
We're all brothers here.

67
00:04:34,770 --> 00:04:35,320
Get up.

68
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:36,940
No need for all these formalities.

69
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:37,760
Get up, get up.

70
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:40,560
Come on.

71
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,040
Let me have a good look at you.

72
00:04:43,110 --> 00:04:44,100
You're still so small.

73
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:45,360
Why haven't you grown?

74
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,900
Are you not eating enough?

75
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:50,220
What are you laughing at?

76
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:53,320
Have you been
practicing riding and archery lately?

77
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:53,960
Yes.

78
00:04:54,650 --> 00:04:56,050
Don't slack off, hear me?

79
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:01,560
Zhanyu, why are you still kneeling?

80
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:02,080
Get up.

81
00:05:08,470 --> 00:05:09,680
I told you to get up.

82
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:10,260
Get up.

83
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,000
Being pigheaded with me, huh?

84
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:18,560
Get up.

85
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:20,050
What's wrong this time?

86
00:05:20,050 --> 00:05:22,940
[Young Zhu Zhanyu,
Fifth Son of the Prince of Han]

87
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:21,500
Your father beat you?

88
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:25,230
Get up.

89
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:27,960
Get up.

90
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:31,120
What's the meaning of this?

91
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:31,640
Get up.

92
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:38,940
You're my dear younger brother.

93
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:40,630
Brothers are as close as
one's own hands and feet.

94
00:05:40,630 --> 00:05:41,680
Your father doesn't dote on you,

95
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:42,220
but I do.

96
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:44,000
Give me a smile.

97
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,240
One more smile.

98
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,180
That's more like it.

99
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:48,710
Alright.

100
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,030
Today,

101
00:05:50,590 --> 00:05:51,960
we brothers of the Zhu family

102
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,680
finally have a chance to get together.

103
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,390
Since you've all come to the palace,

104
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:56,390
I should of course

105
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,290
host a banquet for you.

106
00:05:58,290 --> 00:06:00,000
We shall drink until none of us can stand!

107
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:00,410
Let's go.

108
00:06:00,410 --> 00:06:01,090
Let's go!

109
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:02,150
Come on!

110
00:06:02,650 --> 00:06:03,710
Let's go!

111
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:07,230
Let's go!

112
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:30,910
I'll never forget

113
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:32,640
the way he looked at me then.

114
00:06:34,330 --> 00:06:35,390
It's been 10 years.

115
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:38,450
I've been watching him
for 10 years since then.

116
00:06:39,090 --> 00:06:40,620
I'll never come here again.

117
00:06:43,350 --> 00:06:46,080
Unless you, Father,
are seated upon that throne.

118
00:06:49,270 --> 00:06:51,220
Set off for Huai'an immediately.

119
00:06:51,590 --> 00:06:53,440
Bring back Zhu Zhanji's head

120
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,280
and hand it to me personally.

121
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:56,110
Yes, Father.

122
00:07:11,230 --> 00:07:12,090
Your Highness,

123
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:13,710
the rain is getting heavier.

124
00:07:13,710 --> 00:07:15,370
You still have an arrow wound.

125
00:07:15,410 --> 00:07:16,710
Let's get inside.

126
00:07:25,270 --> 00:07:27,870
Then I'll stand in the rain
with Your Highness.

127
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:30,830
Tell me,

128
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,620
with his injuries,

129
00:07:33,710 --> 00:07:35,110
can he make it to Beijing?

130
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:37,440
Whether he can make it to Beijing

131
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:39,120
is beyond our control.

132
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,000
You've become

133
00:07:43,270 --> 00:07:44,520
rather blunt lately.

134
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:49,380
It's not that I'd dare say
just anything to you bluntly.

135
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:51,240
I just don't want to lie to myself.

136
00:07:59,140 --> 00:07:59,760
Yu Qian.

137
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:01,190
Yes, Your Highness.

138
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:04,820
If you were in the capital
overseeing state affairs,

139
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:06,560
and the Emperor were critically ill

140
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,680
while I was away

141
00:08:08,030 --> 00:08:09,630
and there was no word from me,

142
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:10,960
what would you do?

143
00:08:13,350 --> 00:08:15,610
I would petition Her Majesty the Empress

144
00:08:15,830 --> 00:08:18,560
to have the Prince of Yue act as regent,

145
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:21,450
and then search for the Crown Prince.

146
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,380
And if your search proved fruitless?

147
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:35,870
Then I'd

148
00:08:36,250 --> 00:08:39,049
support the Prince of Yue
in ascending the throne.

149
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:51,330
I'm only missing,

150
00:08:52,730 --> 00:08:53,990
not dead.

151
00:08:55,350 --> 00:08:58,080
The throne cannot
remain vacant for a single day.

152
00:08:58,130 --> 00:08:58,990
Mencius said,

153
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:02,560
"The people come first, the state second,
and the ruler last."

154
00:09:03,010 --> 00:09:04,870
That's the way to govern a nation.

155
00:09:14,870 --> 00:09:15,510
Indeed.

156
00:09:16,490 --> 00:09:18,350
The ruler is the least important.

157
00:09:23,470 --> 00:09:25,530
As long as the Ming Empire endures...

158
00:09:25,590 --> 00:09:28,400
At present, very few people know

159
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:30,330
that Your Highness is still alive.

160
00:09:30,750 --> 00:09:32,080
The officials don't know,

161
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,510
the imperial family doesn't know,

162
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:35,570
and the common people know even less.

163
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,420
So they must act according to the rites

164
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,380
and the laws of the state.

165
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:39,670
Then what are the laws of the state?

166
00:09:39,670 --> 00:09:41,870
It's not a matter of personal feelings.

167
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:45,130
The law must remain impartial,
whatever anyone feels.

168
00:09:45,130 --> 00:09:46,700
It's a system of rules
designed to prevent treacherous men

169
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:50,630
from throwing the government
into disorder when the realm is in peril.

170
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:54,870
I understand.

171
00:09:58,920 --> 00:09:59,750
You're right.

172
00:10:05,450 --> 00:10:06,780
"The people come first,

173
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:09,470
the state second,

174
00:10:11,830 --> 00:10:12,960
and the ruler last."

175
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:15,860
[Countdown: 14 days]

176
00:10:21,550 --> 00:10:24,500
[An Abandoned Workshop in Yangzhou]

177
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:50,710
Lord Yu.

178
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:52,640
Take the Crown Prince to that room.

179
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:53,140
Okay.

180
00:11:00,730 --> 00:11:01,590
Your Highness.

181
00:11:22,010 --> 00:11:22,870
Your Highness.

182
00:11:24,090 --> 00:11:24,960
Please make do.

183
00:11:45,230 --> 00:11:46,090
Your Highness,

184
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,470
-From now on,
-I...

185
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,920
you may call me Young Master Hong Wang.

186
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:56,280
Hong Wang...

187
00:11:57,330 --> 00:11:58,130
Young Master.

188
00:11:59,290 --> 00:12:00,890
Please rest here for a while.

189
00:12:01,630 --> 00:12:04,490
Wu Dingyuan and I will go to
Guazhou Ferry Wharf now.

190
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:05,710
Just like that?

191
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:08,230
Canal transport has its own system:

192
00:12:08,350 --> 00:12:09,510
the Canal Transport Commander,

193
00:12:09,510 --> 00:12:11,320
the River Affairs Office, and so on.

194
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:14,320
Have you figured out
the relationships between them?

195
00:12:14,830 --> 00:12:16,890
Getting a grasp of those connections

196
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:17,920
is not difficult.

197
00:12:18,750 --> 00:12:19,610
The key thing is

198
00:12:19,630 --> 00:12:22,180
the salt merchants, grain dealers,
moneylenders, and pawnshop owners

199
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:23,370
pulling the strings behind the scenes.

200
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:26,430
The power dynamics among them
are incredibly complex.

201
00:12:29,110 --> 00:12:30,470
Finding a tribute vessel

202
00:12:30,470 --> 00:12:32,530
that can carry the four of us in secret

203
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:35,260
definitely won't be easy.

204
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:38,360
Old Mule is right.

205
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:41,560
If we just go and ask,

206
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:45,930
they'll all claim to be
law-abiding boat officers.

207
00:12:45,930 --> 00:12:47,330
We won't learn anything.

208
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:49,220
Then what do you suggest?

209
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:54,450
Once we figure out how this trade works,

210
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:56,900
it'll naturally get easier.

211
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:58,940
And how does it work, exactly?

212
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,000
Rectifier Yu.

213
00:13:02,710 --> 00:13:03,400
Follow him.

214
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:05,680
Yes.

215
00:13:16,350 --> 00:13:17,080
Dr. Su,

216
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,080
please take good care of my young master.

217
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:19,590
Who?

218
00:13:20,330 --> 00:13:21,330
The Crown Prince.

219
00:13:21,850 --> 00:13:23,040
From now on, we just address him

220
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:23,970
as Young Master.

221
00:13:24,630 --> 00:13:25,230
Thank you.

222
00:13:25,610 --> 00:13:26,470
Leave him to me.

223
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,360
Young Master.

224
00:14:14,090 --> 00:14:15,350
Here's some hot water.

225
00:14:35,650 --> 00:14:43,660
♪ Across heaven and earth, as the winds
wander, when shall I return home? ♪

226
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:52,160
♪ Against a fate I can't fathom,
who is truly my foe? ♪

227
00:14:52,320 --> 00:15:00,410
♪ Where shall tomorrow lead me,
and who will share my cup? ♪

228
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:08,420
♪ The northern sky stretches wide,
with one lone star aglow ♪

229
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:13,910
♪ Life's journey is but a fleeting dream ♪

230
00:15:15,090 --> 00:15:18,910
♪ In this turbulent age,
all things pass in haste ♪

231
00:15:19,830 --> 00:15:23,570
♪ I wonder what may come
and how things will be ♪

232
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:31,130
♪ Waves rise high,
with storms brewing below ♪

233
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:36,160
♪ With my blade turned north,
I chart my course by the stars ♪

234
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:41,570
♪ I've seen it all,
love and hate entwined ♪

235
00:15:42,450 --> 00:15:50,530
♪ Across heaven and earth, as the winds
wander, when shall I return home? ♪

236
00:15:50,770 --> 00:15:58,730
♪ Against a fate I can't fathom,
who is truly my foe? ♪

237
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:07,170
♪ Where shall tomorrow lead me,
and who will share my cup? ♪

238
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:15,140
♪ The northern sky stretches wide,
with one lone star aglow ♪

239
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:57,260
♪ Across heaven and earth,
your name shall grace an age of peace ♪

240
00:16:57,580 --> 00:17:04,690
♪ My boat drifts on,
as old friends fade from memory ♪

241
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:14,140
♪ Joy and sorrow, loss and gain,
flow like an endless river ♪

242
00:17:10,069 --> 00:17:10,869
Young Master.

243
00:17:11,569 --> 00:17:12,369
Young Master!

244
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:14,230
Young Master!

245
00:17:14,230 --> 00:17:22,260
♪ Distant as a lone star,
light as a passing dream ♪

246
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:42,760
Your Highness,

247
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:45,500
if you pull out the arrowhead like this,

248
00:17:45,660 --> 00:17:46,920
you'll lose your life.

249
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:14,000
Pull the arrowhead out for me.

250
00:18:23,710 --> 00:18:25,440
If you want to die, that's easy.

251
00:18:26,190 --> 00:18:27,100
I'll help you.

252
00:18:29,930 --> 00:18:31,530
But if you die just like this,

253
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:33,060
how will you face the dead?

254
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,360
Someone wanted you dead,

255
00:18:35,650 --> 00:18:37,910
and a whole boatload of people were lost.

256
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:39,840
Pull the arrowhead out.

257
00:18:39,890 --> 00:18:40,690
In this world,

258
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:42,940
people can be gone in the blink of an eye.

259
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:44,860
Yet those who remain must go on living.

260
00:18:44,860 --> 00:18:47,580
Can you hear the bereaved families crying?

261
00:18:50,790 --> 00:18:52,750
And those who died for you—

262
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,960
have you ever dreamed of them?

263
00:18:56,230 --> 00:18:59,490
Do you still remember
what your grandfather once told you?

264
00:18:59,620 --> 00:19:00,900
Never forget them.

265
00:19:03,710 --> 00:19:04,380
Don't move.

266
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:27,940
Part of the arrowhead broke off.

267
00:19:41,090 --> 00:19:42,620
You were dreaming just now,

268
00:19:42,860 --> 00:19:44,260
shouting the whole time.

269
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,210
I've stopped the bleeding.

270
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,230
Although a piece of
the arrowhead broke off,

271
00:19:51,230 --> 00:19:52,960
it won't affect your movement.

272
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:54,390
Don't worry.

273
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:56,070
With me along on this journey,

274
00:19:56,070 --> 00:19:57,670
there won't be any problems.

275
00:19:57,880 --> 00:19:58,680
Thank you.

276
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:01,000
It's my duty.

277
00:20:02,750 --> 00:20:04,510
There aren't many herbs in this workshop.

278
00:20:04,510 --> 00:20:06,920
I've boiled
some honeysuckle and dandelion,

279
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:09,340
both good for
reducing swelling and easing pain.

280
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:09,840
Here.

281
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:13,480
I'll drink it myself.

282
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:26,160
Good medicine always tastes bitter.

283
00:21:09,990 --> 00:21:10,710
You brat!

284
00:21:10,790 --> 00:21:12,440
I'll beat you to death!

285
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:14,530
Stop hitting me.

286
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:16,660
I...

287
00:21:17,030 --> 00:21:18,440
I'll catch you!

288
00:21:18,570 --> 00:21:20,270
I'll beat you to death!

289
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:22,180
Beat you to death!

290
00:21:22,770 --> 00:21:23,550
You brat!

291
00:21:23,570 --> 00:21:24,970
You're driving me crazy!

292
00:21:28,010 --> 00:21:28,750
Still trying to run?

293
00:21:28,750 --> 00:21:29,730
I'll beat you to death!

294
00:21:29,730 --> 00:21:30,420
Please stop.

295
00:21:30,420 --> 00:21:31,280
It hurts, Papa!

296
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:33,530
Papa,

297
00:21:33,820 --> 00:21:36,010
you don't need to worry about that at all.

298
00:21:36,010 --> 00:21:37,140
If you die one day,

299
00:21:37,290 --> 00:21:39,160
I'll definitely piece you back together

300
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,530
and give you a grand funeral.

301
00:21:40,530 --> 00:21:41,510
I'll never let

302
00:21:41,530 --> 00:21:43,290
your soul wander alone

303
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:44,990
out there.

304
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:46,550
Is that any way to talk?

305
00:21:46,790 --> 00:21:47,360
Come on!

306
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:28,490
Good-for-Nothing,

307
00:22:28,510 --> 00:22:29,310
let's hear it.

308
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:31,240
How does this trade work?

309
00:22:31,700 --> 00:22:33,330
First of all, it takes money.

310
00:22:34,120 --> 00:22:35,680
Owners of private boats

311
00:22:35,790 --> 00:22:37,120
usually have to pay a fee

312
00:22:37,380 --> 00:22:39,070
to the local brokers

313
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:41,290
if they want to dock without trouble.

314
00:22:41,290 --> 00:22:41,960
So

315
00:22:42,210 --> 00:22:43,100
the brokers are the ones

316
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:44,700
who know all the ins and outs.

317
00:22:44,750 --> 00:22:47,550
They know better than anyone what's
going on with every boat at the wharf.

318
00:22:47,550 --> 00:22:48,770
As long as we bribe one of them

319
00:22:48,770 --> 00:22:51,230
and get him to
put us in touch with the right people,

320
00:22:51,230 --> 00:22:52,770
he can act as
a go-between and negotiate for us.

321
00:22:52,770 --> 00:22:54,830
We'll find a suitable boat in no time.

322
00:22:56,950 --> 00:23:04,650
♪ Boats lie moored at Guazhou Ferry Wharf ♪

323
00:23:02,910 --> 00:23:07,450
[Guazhou Ferry, Yangzhou]

324
00:23:05,510 --> 00:23:13,210
♪ Tribute ships are laden with
fresh goods ♪

325
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:13,230
Excuse me.

326
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:15,440
May I ask if your chief broker is here?

327
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:21,920
♪ Brokers and their chiefs
haggle over their deals ♪

328
00:23:19,210 --> 00:23:20,740
Someone is looking for you!

329
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:34,210
♪ The entire world bustles,
chasing profit ♪

330
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:25,470
Sir.

331
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:28,960
We'd like to...

332
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:30,770
We'd like to go to Beijing.

333
00:23:31,550 --> 00:23:32,270
And then...

334
00:23:33,490 --> 00:23:34,310
And then we might need to...

335
00:23:34,310 --> 00:23:35,970
need to secretly take a few...

336
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:37,470
Well...

337
00:23:40,510 --> 00:23:41,640
How should we say it?

338
00:23:42,540 --> 00:23:44,490
Do you have a route to the east bank?

339
00:23:45,790 --> 00:23:46,960
Of course we do.

340
00:23:48,210 --> 00:23:50,010
May I ask how you want to cross it?

341
00:23:50,540 --> 00:23:51,780
Four cormorants,

342
00:23:51,810 --> 00:23:52,770
all with their necks tied up.

343
00:23:52,770 --> 00:23:54,460
What nonsense are you talking about?

344
00:23:54,460 --> 00:23:55,550
We need a boat.

345
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:56,650
Why are you talking about birds?

346
00:23:56,650 --> 00:23:57,970
Can you stop yapping?

347
00:23:58,060 --> 00:23:59,590
If you're so good, you do it.

348
00:24:00,210 --> 00:24:01,120
Without cargo,

349
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:03,330
the ship owner won't get a share,

350
00:24:03,330 --> 00:24:05,420
so the price will be higher.

351
00:24:06,130 --> 00:24:07,130
What kind of boat?

352
00:24:07,380 --> 00:24:08,380
A tribute vessel.

353
00:24:12,470 --> 00:24:13,800
The price is no problem.

354
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:15,600
But we need it quickly.

355
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:16,260
Tonight...

356
00:24:16,940 --> 00:24:18,050
Or tomorrow morning at the latest.

357
00:24:18,050 --> 00:24:19,050
We must depart by then.

358
00:24:19,050 --> 00:24:20,250
Can you arrange that?

359
00:24:20,870 --> 00:24:23,310
There's a suitable one
right here at the wharf.

360
00:24:23,310 --> 00:24:24,750
Tomorrow around 3 AM,

361
00:24:25,120 --> 00:24:26,380
the handover will be completed

362
00:24:26,380 --> 00:24:28,310
and the ship brought in to the dock.

363
00:24:31,990 --> 00:24:32,790
May we...

364
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:35,160
have a word with the owner?

365
00:24:36,610 --> 00:24:37,110
Okay.

366
00:24:38,430 --> 00:24:38,910
Come with me.

367
00:24:38,910 --> 00:24:39,440
Let's go.

368
00:24:39,630 --> 00:24:40,230
Follow me.

369
00:24:42,500 --> 00:24:44,900
[Xie Sanfa, Boat Owner]

370
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:44,020
Keep hauling, everyone.

371
00:24:44,050 --> 00:24:45,390
Put your backs into it.

372
00:24:45,680 --> 00:24:48,810
The Emperor is waiting for
his first taste of the season.

373
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:50,250
These two are in a hurry,

374
00:24:50,270 --> 00:24:51,930
which means good money for us.

375
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:53,020
Gentlemen,

376
00:24:53,230 --> 00:24:54,460
this is the ship owner,

377
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:55,310
Mr. Xie Sanfa.

378
00:24:55,770 --> 00:24:57,830
You can discuss the details with him.

379
00:24:59,120 --> 00:25:01,470
There will be 4 people, you say?

380
00:25:01,640 --> 00:25:02,600
Yes, 4 people.

381
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:06,360
Ten taels?

382
00:25:06,810 --> 00:25:07,870
One hundred taels.

383
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:08,940
Are you robbing us?

384
00:25:09,770 --> 00:25:12,170
If you can't afford it,
go ask someone else.

385
00:25:14,100 --> 00:25:14,750
Let's go.

386
00:25:14,780 --> 00:25:16,810
Didn't we just ask another ship owner?

387
00:25:16,810 --> 00:25:17,770
His price was much more reasonable.

388
00:25:17,770 --> 00:25:19,030
No need to waste our time with him.

389
00:25:19,030 --> 00:25:20,140
When did we find another one?

390
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:20,870
Just pay him.

391
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:21,470
Let's go.

392
00:25:22,930 --> 00:25:24,130
Hey, Little Xingren!

393
00:25:26,130 --> 00:25:28,730
-What an idiot.
-One hundred taels it is, then.

394
00:25:28,940 --> 00:25:29,460
Here.

395
00:25:30,170 --> 00:25:31,060
Keep

396
00:25:31,620 --> 00:25:32,310
the change.

397
00:25:33,860 --> 00:25:34,730
Straightforward.

398
00:25:34,730 --> 00:25:37,060
So, can we really leave tomorrow morning?

399
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:39,840
This vessel is carrying fresh produce.

400
00:25:40,060 --> 00:25:42,460
We must set sail before daybreak tomorrow.

401
00:25:51,840 --> 00:25:52,440
Thanks.

402
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:56,840
Here, take this back.

403
00:25:57,120 --> 00:25:58,270
You're no pro,

404
00:25:58,530 --> 00:25:59,790
but you had to show off.

405
00:26:00,180 --> 00:26:00,910
Impressive.

406
00:26:02,790 --> 00:26:04,880
I didn't expect things to go

407
00:26:05,270 --> 00:26:06,240
so smoothly.

408
00:26:07,940 --> 00:26:10,600
Let's hurry back
and report to the young master.

409
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:13,400
What?

410
00:26:14,510 --> 00:26:16,880
Well, aren't you the capable one?

411
00:26:17,530 --> 00:26:18,730
From now on, you don't

412
00:26:18,840 --> 00:26:20,500
need to ask me about anything.

413
00:26:21,350 --> 00:26:23,550
Didn't you say we needed to spend money?

414
00:26:25,280 --> 00:26:27,410
You think I stole your thunder, right?

415
00:26:29,140 --> 00:26:31,010
"Jingkou and Guazhou are separated
by only a stretch of water;

416
00:26:31,010 --> 00:26:32,850
Zhongshan is just a few mountains away."

417
00:26:32,850 --> 00:26:35,400
We may not possess
the lofty vision of Wang Anshi,

418
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:37,800
but for the sake of
the people and the state,

419
00:26:37,860 --> 00:26:39,460
we should at least be open and honorable,

420
00:26:39,460 --> 00:26:40,260
shouldn't we?

421
00:26:42,070 --> 00:26:42,680
Oh, you,

422
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:44,710
don't give me
that pedantic literary nonsense.

423
00:26:44,710 --> 00:26:46,200
I don't understand a word of it.

424
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:48,060
You're just wasting your breath.

425
00:26:48,230 --> 00:26:49,250
Surely you understand

426
00:26:49,250 --> 00:26:50,840
that a grown man should stand tall

427
00:26:50,840 --> 00:26:52,380
and live honorably
between heaven and earth?

428
00:26:52,380 --> 00:26:54,490
I only know the Heaven and Earth tiles.

429
00:26:54,490 --> 00:26:56,290
What kind of tile is
"standing between Heaven and Earth"?

430
00:26:56,290 --> 00:26:57,440
Teach me later.

431
00:26:58,660 --> 00:26:59,470
Vulgar.

432
00:27:00,380 --> 00:27:01,550
Utterly vulgar.

433
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:04,070
Without this vulgar man,

434
00:27:04,510 --> 00:27:06,060
you'd all be dead by now.

435
00:27:06,840 --> 00:27:08,860
You think I want to travel with you?

436
00:27:09,220 --> 00:27:09,950
Out of my way.

437
00:27:11,570 --> 00:27:12,700
Where are you going?

438
00:27:13,350 --> 00:27:14,680
That's not the way back.

439
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:25,680
What?

440
00:27:26,640 --> 00:27:27,840
You don't trust them?

441
00:27:28,310 --> 00:27:30,550
They found us a ship just like that,

442
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:33,880
and we can leave
first thing tomorrow morning?

443
00:27:33,880 --> 00:27:36,600
Since when does anything work out
that conveniently?

444
00:27:36,600 --> 00:27:38,260
If you got that lucky at cards,

445
00:27:38,780 --> 00:27:40,310
someone would be cheating.

446
00:27:48,700 --> 00:27:50,310
If you have a question,
ask them to their faces.

447
00:27:50,310 --> 00:27:51,640
Sneaking back like this

448
00:27:52,250 --> 00:27:53,980
is not how a gentleman behaves.

449
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:56,450
You can never tell
what's in a man's heart.

450
00:27:56,880 --> 00:27:57,840
What would

451
00:27:57,860 --> 00:27:58,790
you know anyway?

452
00:28:12,710 --> 00:28:13,270
Man,

453
00:28:13,890 --> 00:28:15,340
how long will it take to load all this?

454
00:28:15,340 --> 00:28:17,380
Probably until sunset.

455
00:28:23,010 --> 00:28:24,790
Xie Sanfa doesn't look like

456
00:28:24,910 --> 00:28:25,890
a local to me.

457
00:28:25,910 --> 00:28:27,710
Right, they came from Zhoushan.

458
00:28:28,180 --> 00:28:29,780
How long have they been here?

459
00:28:30,420 --> 00:28:31,210
Four or five days.

460
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:32,210
Four or five days?

461
00:28:32,490 --> 00:28:32,960
Yeah.

462
00:28:33,710 --> 00:28:35,270
And the boat still hasn't left?

463
00:28:35,270 --> 00:28:36,530
Won't the fresh tribute goods

464
00:28:36,530 --> 00:28:37,510
spoil soon?

465
00:28:37,710 --> 00:28:38,400
Exactly.

466
00:28:38,570 --> 00:28:40,030
They're very anxious too.

467
00:28:41,750 --> 00:28:42,270
Man.

468
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:44,960
Here, get yourself a bowl of noodles.

469
00:28:44,960 --> 00:28:45,820
Thank you, sir.

470
00:28:47,470 --> 00:28:49,300
Well, does Xie Sanfa

471
00:28:49,550 --> 00:28:50,790
have two buddies?

472
00:28:51,210 --> 00:28:51,620
Yes, yes, yes.

473
00:28:51,620 --> 00:28:53,420
The three of them came together.

474
00:29:03,890 --> 00:29:06,210
You're making caulking materials, right?

475
00:29:06,210 --> 00:29:06,750
Yes.

476
00:29:07,490 --> 00:29:08,310
You use it to seal

477
00:29:08,310 --> 00:29:09,380
leaks in the hull, right?

478
00:29:09,380 --> 00:29:10,440
Yes, that's right.

479
00:29:11,100 --> 00:29:12,360
Which ship is leaking?

480
00:29:12,750 --> 00:29:14,120
The one up ahead.

481
00:29:15,620 --> 00:29:16,270
That one?

482
00:29:17,340 --> 00:29:18,510
Isn't that boat supposed to set sail

483
00:29:18,510 --> 00:29:19,960
before dawn tomorrow?

484
00:29:20,380 --> 00:29:21,640
That, I wouldn't know.

485
00:29:27,470 --> 00:29:28,820
Son of a bitch.

486
00:29:32,970 --> 00:29:37,070
[Boatman Zheng Xianti]

487
00:29:33,110 --> 00:29:34,450
Mr. Xie really pulled a clever one.

488
00:29:34,450 --> 00:29:36,050
It got us out of an emergency,

489
00:29:36,050 --> 00:29:37,360
and now we can face everyone back home.

490
00:29:37,070 --> 00:29:40,500
[Boatman Zheng Xianlun]

491
00:29:38,810 --> 00:29:41,140
It's just a bit unfair
to those two guests.

492
00:29:48,050 --> 00:29:49,850
Please spare our lives, heroes.

493
00:29:50,100 --> 00:29:51,750
Carters, boatmen, innkeepers,
porters, and brokers

494
00:29:51,750 --> 00:29:53,360
deserve death even if innocent!

495
00:29:53,360 --> 00:29:55,160
You two are porters and brokers.

496
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:56,660
You deserve to die,

497
00:29:56,680 --> 00:29:57,290
understood?

498
00:29:57,290 --> 00:29:58,750
Even if we were blind and wicked,

499
00:29:58,750 --> 00:29:59,620
and sinners in a past life,

500
00:29:59,620 --> 00:30:01,290
we wouldn't dare scheme against you.

501
00:30:01,290 --> 00:30:02,950
We have our difficulties too.

502
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:04,160
In this world,

503
00:30:04,460 --> 00:30:06,260
who doesn't have difficulties?

504
00:30:07,250 --> 00:30:07,750
Heroes,

505
00:30:08,310 --> 00:30:09,470
I swear to heaven.

506
00:30:10,180 --> 00:30:12,660
Ever since the Canal Transport Office
changed the regulations,

507
00:30:12,660 --> 00:30:13,440
we've barely

508
00:30:14,070 --> 00:30:15,220
been able to make a living.

509
00:30:15,220 --> 00:30:17,150
What regulations did they change?

510
00:30:18,010 --> 00:30:18,700
The canal transport

511
00:30:18,700 --> 00:30:20,160
used to operate
under the relay transport system.

512
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:20,980
But after the regulations changed,

513
00:30:20,980 --> 00:30:22,310
it became a transshipment system.

514
00:30:22,310 --> 00:30:23,880
This was promulgated
less than half a month ago.

515
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:26,310
We only learned of it
upon reaching Yangzhou.

516
00:30:26,310 --> 00:30:27,270
Get to the point.

517
00:30:29,440 --> 00:30:30,550
Under the new rules,

518
00:30:30,550 --> 00:30:32,960
civilian vessels
coming from Jiangnan, Huguang, and Jiangxi

519
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:34,200
are no longer
allowed to sail the entire route.

520
00:30:34,200 --> 00:30:35,750
They only need to
go to the Huai'an granary

521
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:36,880
and transfer the goods to

522
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:38,810
the 24 guard stations in Jiangbei.

523
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:41,200
Then government vessels will
transport them directly to the capital.

524
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:44,120
Isn't that supposed to
ease the burden on the people?

525
00:30:44,120 --> 00:30:45,120
That may be so,

526
00:30:45,680 --> 00:30:48,470
but the transport fee
from Huai'an to Dezhou

527
00:30:48,700 --> 00:30:50,270
must be paid by us ship owners.

528
00:30:50,270 --> 00:30:51,030
And this fee

529
00:30:51,230 --> 00:30:53,380
is more than 5 times higher than before.

530
00:30:53,380 --> 00:30:54,200
The three of us

531
00:30:54,220 --> 00:30:55,370
bought fresh goods from Zhoushan.

532
00:30:55,370 --> 00:30:55,990
Then, when we reached Yangzhou,

533
00:30:55,990 --> 00:30:57,090
we found that the regulations
had suddenly changed.

534
00:30:57,090 --> 00:30:58,920
We simply couldn't afford the extra cost.

535
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:00,750
All we could do was watch the goods

536
00:31:00,750 --> 00:31:01,250
rot

537
00:31:01,550 --> 00:31:02,160
and stink.

538
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:07,550
So that 100 taels you charged us

539
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:08,920
was really a toll?

540
00:31:10,070 --> 00:31:10,960
Not exactly.

541
00:31:12,130 --> 00:31:13,640
Mr. Xie really had no other choice,

542
00:31:13,640 --> 00:31:15,120
so he came up with this idea.

543
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:16,320
The villagers pooled

544
00:31:16,340 --> 00:31:17,210
their money to buy

545
00:31:17,210 --> 00:31:18,600
the fresh goods.

546
00:31:19,030 --> 00:31:20,690
We have to answer to everyone.

547
00:31:21,920 --> 00:31:23,940
Right now, Mr. Xie is
at the Canal Transport Office.

548
00:31:23,940 --> 00:31:25,180
If he can reach an agreement with them,

549
00:31:25,180 --> 00:31:26,210
we'll load the ship immediately,

550
00:31:26,210 --> 00:31:27,580
and you'll be able to head north with us.

551
00:31:27,580 --> 00:31:29,510
And if he can't reach an agreement?

552
00:31:29,790 --> 00:31:30,550
Don't worry.

553
00:31:31,120 --> 00:31:32,070
Knowing Mr. Xie,

554
00:31:32,470 --> 00:31:33,870
I'm certain he'll return

555
00:31:34,510 --> 00:31:35,440
every last coin.

556
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:43,230
Go on, then.

557
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:49,140
I know you're anxious.

558
00:31:49,230 --> 00:31:51,510
Your fresh goods
won't keep much longer, huh?

559
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:52,590
Follow me to get the letter of passage,

560
00:31:52,590 --> 00:31:53,680
and tomorrow you can set out.

561
00:31:53,680 --> 00:31:54,480
Yes, yes, yes.

562
00:31:54,550 --> 00:31:55,510
Thank you for your consideration, My Lord.

563
00:31:55,510 --> 00:31:56,570
My consideration?

564
00:31:56,610 --> 00:31:59,810
It's all thanks to
the kindness of the Assistant Prefect.

565
00:32:00,270 --> 00:32:01,300
Come with me to collect the letter,

566
00:32:01,300 --> 00:32:02,900
and you can set sail tomorrow.

567
00:32:02,900 --> 00:32:03,510
Yes.

568
00:32:03,710 --> 00:32:04,840
Then please convey my thanks

569
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:06,770
to the Assistant Prefect, My Lord.

570
00:32:12,310 --> 00:32:12,920
My Lord,

571
00:32:13,550 --> 00:32:16,850
t-this is where Guazhou dumps its waste.

572
00:32:17,700 --> 00:32:18,890
Why bring me here?

573
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:21,190
Since I've walked so far with you,

574
00:32:21,550 --> 00:32:23,610
shouldn't you give me some tea money?

575
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:26,550
My Lord,

576
00:32:26,940 --> 00:32:28,540
you're from the government.

577
00:32:28,970 --> 00:32:29,810
You can't

578
00:32:29,830 --> 00:32:31,160
rob me like this.

579
00:32:31,360 --> 00:32:33,250
The waters around Guazhou are treacherous.

580
00:32:33,250 --> 00:32:34,360
Every year, a few

581
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:36,160
clueless outsiders drown here.

582
00:32:36,680 --> 00:32:38,750
Even the Dragon King
can't do anything about it.

583
00:32:38,750 --> 00:32:39,680
My Lord, My Lord,

584
00:32:39,680 --> 00:32:40,880
I'm just a fisherman.

585
00:32:40,970 --> 00:32:42,370
I don't have anything...

586
00:32:58,200 --> 00:33:00,060
He's already paid what he should!

587
00:33:00,600 --> 00:33:01,940
Why are you still bullying him?

588
00:33:01,940 --> 00:33:02,440
Speak!

589
00:33:02,460 --> 00:33:03,790
I'll speak, I'll speak.

590
00:33:04,030 --> 00:33:06,070
Sir, I'll speak.

591
00:33:07,290 --> 00:33:07,850
Speak!

592
00:33:11,310 --> 00:33:12,310
Sirs,

593
00:33:12,570 --> 00:33:15,170
you wouldn't know
unless you work on the river.

594
00:33:15,470 --> 00:33:17,670
It's only the middle of the fifth month.

595
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:20,160
The canal's water level
is just six-tenths,

596
00:33:21,120 --> 00:33:23,640
so very few ships can set sail.

597
00:33:23,990 --> 00:33:25,970
We have to wait
until after the sixth month,

598
00:33:25,970 --> 00:33:27,660
when the summer wheat
is harvested everywhere,

599
00:33:27,660 --> 00:33:29,530
and water is released into the canal.

600
00:33:29,530 --> 00:33:31,360
Only when it reaches nine-tenths

601
00:33:31,360 --> 00:33:33,230
can the ships be sent out
in large numbers.

602
00:33:33,230 --> 00:33:34,310
So now...

603
00:33:34,640 --> 00:33:35,640
Get to the point.

604
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:37,360
The point is,

605
00:33:37,470 --> 00:33:39,800
I don't have any letter of passage either.

606
00:33:40,230 --> 00:33:41,090
Even if you pay,

607
00:33:41,170 --> 00:33:43,100
you still won't be able to set sail.

608
00:33:44,290 --> 00:33:44,990
But...

609
00:33:45,180 --> 00:33:46,210
-But what?
-But...

610
00:33:46,210 --> 00:33:46,930
Hurry up and say it!

611
00:33:46,930 --> 00:33:47,960
But... But...

612
00:33:48,810 --> 00:33:51,210
the ships heading north
from Guazhou to Huai'an

613
00:33:51,210 --> 00:33:53,200
are all under the control of
the Yangzhou authorities.

614
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:55,680
They usually allocate
some of their letters of passage

615
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:57,750
to powerful local families.

616
00:33:58,710 --> 00:33:59,680
Then, to get a letter of passage,

617
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:01,680
which families should we approach?

618
00:34:01,710 --> 00:34:03,240
The Xu family of Songjiang,

619
00:34:03,660 --> 00:34:04,990
the He family of Huzhou,

620
00:34:05,570 --> 00:34:07,030
the Qian family of Haiyan,

621
00:34:07,100 --> 00:34:08,429
the Gu family of Kuaiji,

622
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:09,920
and...

623
00:34:11,310 --> 00:34:12,860
Hey, you! You!

624
00:34:13,340 --> 00:34:15,900
T-The gambling den you always go to...

625
00:34:16,070 --> 00:34:17,670
Didn't you say there's cricket fighting?

626
00:34:17,670 --> 00:34:19,360
Have they posted the notice yet?

627
00:34:19,360 --> 00:34:20,900
They posted it first thing this morning.

628
00:34:20,900 --> 00:34:22,300
There's a match tonight.

629
00:34:22,630 --> 00:34:23,760
I was still planning

630
00:34:24,300 --> 00:34:25,230
to go try my luck.

631
00:34:26,190 --> 00:34:27,310
Look at you, sirs.

632
00:34:28,219 --> 00:34:29,960
You must be averse to killing.

633
00:34:30,409 --> 00:34:31,840
Hasn't the instant karma...

634
00:34:31,840 --> 00:34:34,130
The instant good karma has come knocking!

635
00:34:34,130 --> 00:34:35,219
W-What do you mean?

636
00:34:35,760 --> 00:34:37,280
There's a gambling den here,

637
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:40,460
and it's cricket-fighting season.

638
00:34:41,170 --> 00:34:42,710
And now that they've posted the notice,

639
00:34:42,710 --> 00:34:45,239
cricket gamblers
from far and near will come.

640
00:34:45,719 --> 00:34:46,699
The gambling den

641
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:49,719
is managed by a steward

642
00:34:49,940 --> 00:34:51,800
of a powerful family in Yangzhou.

643
00:34:52,150 --> 00:34:53,030
He loves

644
00:34:53,150 --> 00:34:55,280
cricket fighting more than anything,

645
00:34:55,590 --> 00:34:58,760
wagering dozens or hundreds of
strings of coins at a time.

646
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:00,150
The power behind him

647
00:35:00,240 --> 00:35:01,760
is nothing to scoff at.

648
00:35:02,690 --> 00:35:04,590
If you two are skilled enough,

649
00:35:05,490 --> 00:35:08,240
you might just be able to win

650
00:35:08,460 --> 00:35:10,060
a letter of passage from him.

651
00:35:13,630 --> 00:35:14,760
Whose steward is he?

652
00:35:15,440 --> 00:35:19,440
Naturally, the local "Dragon King"
of Yangzhou:

653
00:35:19,990 --> 00:35:22,990
the Wang family,
salt merchants from Huizhou.

654
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:25,950
The head of the family is Wang Ji.

655
00:37:02,690 --> 00:37:03,490
Young Master.

656
00:37:09,110 --> 00:37:10,170
Let me help you back.

657
00:37:10,170 --> 00:37:10,780
No need.

658
00:37:12,240 --> 00:37:13,440
I can manage on my own.

659
00:37:26,670 --> 00:37:28,720
We can't keep guarding

660
00:37:28,720 --> 00:37:30,650
that abandoned workshop forever.

661
00:37:31,290 --> 00:37:33,690
I've already stationed men near the wharf.

662
00:37:34,070 --> 00:37:35,390
The moment they spot Wu Dingyuan,

663
00:37:35,390 --> 00:37:37,320
they'll report back immediately.

664
00:37:39,540 --> 00:37:40,250
Well...

665
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,400
Just ask what you want to ask.

666
00:37:46,030 --> 00:37:46,680
Envoy,

667
00:37:47,020 --> 00:37:49,020
when we were in Jinling, our mission

668
00:37:49,050 --> 00:37:50,650
was to kill the Crown Prince.

669
00:37:51,190 --> 00:37:52,720
Now that we're in Yangzhou,

670
00:37:52,780 --> 00:37:54,840
why are we suddenly protecting them?

671
00:37:57,900 --> 00:37:59,230
You've got it all wrong.

672
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:03,480
Our Iron Alliance
isn't plotting a rebellion.

673
00:38:05,800 --> 00:38:06,930
The Leader said that

674
00:38:07,440 --> 00:38:09,680
once the Crown Prince's treasure ship
was blown up,

675
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:11,550
we'd never again be lowly commoners,

676
00:38:11,550 --> 00:38:13,750
never again have to hide in the shadows.

677
00:38:17,520 --> 00:38:20,520
And right now, we're not protecting
the Crown Prince,

678
00:38:21,280 --> 00:38:22,720
but Good-for-Nothing.

679
00:38:23,180 --> 00:38:25,240
Could the Leader have made a mistake?

680
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:28,650
How could Good-for-Nothing

681
00:38:28,650 --> 00:38:30,980
possibly be the person we're looking for?

682
00:38:31,850 --> 00:38:33,940
Then why was there no body in the grave?

683
00:38:33,940 --> 00:38:35,010
And why did the Iron Lion refuse to say

684
00:38:35,010 --> 00:38:37,210
a single word, even to his dying breath?

685
00:38:38,510 --> 00:38:40,510
Maybe it's another

686
00:38:41,180 --> 00:38:44,440
crown-prince-switching scheme,
like the ones in novels.

687
00:38:50,440 --> 00:38:51,190
Envoy,

688
00:38:52,110 --> 00:38:52,760
look.

689
00:38:52,990 --> 00:38:54,250
Yangzhou City is huge.

690
00:38:54,570 --> 00:38:55,970
What if we can't find him?

691
00:38:59,200 --> 00:39:00,280
Good-for-Nothing

692
00:39:01,410 --> 00:39:03,220
is with the Crown Prince all day.

693
00:39:04,040 --> 00:39:05,730
So many people want them dead.

694
00:39:06,890 --> 00:39:09,620
The Leader has given the order.
We just follow it.

695
00:39:10,080 --> 00:39:12,220
Anyway, before we figure out who he is,

696
00:39:13,720 --> 00:39:15,380
we must ensure he stays alive.

697
00:39:54,920 --> 00:39:56,820
The transshipment system
was originally introduced

698
00:39:56,820 --> 00:39:58,490
to alleviate the people's burden.

699
00:39:58,490 --> 00:39:59,280
Why

700
00:40:00,860 --> 00:40:02,610
is an extra letter of passage required?

701
00:40:02,610 --> 00:40:03,920
The local authorities keep
inventing pretexts to levy fees.

702
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:06,090
This requirement was created
purely for profit.

703
00:40:06,090 --> 00:40:07,400
Those with power and influence

704
00:40:07,400 --> 00:40:09,730
can travel unimpeded with the letter.

705
00:40:11,670 --> 00:40:13,230
But those without one

706
00:40:13,700 --> 00:40:16,500
have to pay transport fees
at least 5 times higher.

707
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:17,440
Young Master,

708
00:40:18,910 --> 00:40:20,240
at least 5 times higher.

709
00:40:23,010 --> 00:40:24,010
Over time,

710
00:40:25,610 --> 00:40:27,690
the entire canal trade has fallen into

711
00:40:27,690 --> 00:40:30,090
the hands of
a few powerful local families.

712
00:40:32,260 --> 00:40:34,610
A policy meant to ease the people's burden

713
00:40:35,510 --> 00:40:38,110
has instead become
a means of exploiting them.

714
00:40:52,030 --> 00:40:54,160
Why does it smell so strongly of blood?

715
00:40:55,640 --> 00:40:56,750
Dr. Su was just here

716
00:40:56,950 --> 00:40:58,090
treating my wound.

717
00:41:06,530 --> 00:41:07,460
Where is she now?

718
00:41:08,650 --> 00:41:11,650
She said she was going back
to her hometown for a visit.

719
00:41:12,310 --> 00:41:15,240
Didn't she say
the arrowhead couldn't be pulled out?

720
00:41:19,130 --> 00:41:20,790
Fortunately, Dr. Su saved me.

721
00:41:22,810 --> 00:41:24,600
Our top priority is
to return to the capital quickly.

722
00:41:24,600 --> 00:41:26,400
We can no longer get a letter of passage.

723
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:27,760
How about we go by land?

724
00:41:29,440 --> 00:41:30,830
If we go by land,

725
00:41:31,360 --> 00:41:33,620
we won't be able to arrive within 15 days.

726
00:41:33,940 --> 00:41:35,940
Where there's money, there's a way.

727
00:41:36,110 --> 00:41:37,470
Those influential ship owners

728
00:41:37,470 --> 00:41:39,760
just want to make more money.

729
00:41:40,110 --> 00:41:41,840
As long as we have enough money,

730
00:41:42,490 --> 00:41:44,240
we can surely buy a letter of passage.

731
00:41:44,240 --> 00:41:45,500
You don't understand.

732
00:41:47,040 --> 00:41:48,640
There's one powerful family

733
00:41:49,940 --> 00:41:51,800
we absolutely must not approach.

734
00:41:52,180 --> 00:41:53,070
Which family?

735
00:41:54,660 --> 00:41:56,060
The Wang family, Wang Ji.

736
00:41:57,210 --> 00:41:57,870
Who is he?

737
00:42:01,970 --> 00:42:04,620
[Five days earlier]

738
00:42:05,550 --> 00:42:06,410
Your Highness,

739
00:42:06,690 --> 00:42:10,420
Wang Ji, a canal merchant from Yangzhou,
presents a treasure ship.

740
00:42:12,300 --> 00:42:12,970
Mr. Wang,

741
00:42:12,370 --> 00:42:14,320
[Wang Ji, Yangzhou Merchant]

742
00:42:13,440 --> 00:42:15,090
His Highness the Crown Prince
has boarded the treasure ship

743
00:42:15,090 --> 00:42:16,420
and hasn't even had a sip of water.

744
00:42:16,420 --> 00:42:17,950
Quickly, serve the dishes.

745
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:18,640
Yes.

746
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:26,260
Your Highness.

747
00:42:27,690 --> 00:42:40,820
♪ This feast glitters with splendor ♪

748
00:42:28,200 --> 00:42:30,200
This is a famous Yangzhou dish.

749
00:42:31,130 --> 00:42:32,240
We use pork belly,

750
00:42:32,650 --> 00:42:34,340
with just the right balance
of fat and lean meat,

751
00:42:34,340 --> 00:42:36,050
diced into pomegranate-seed-sized pieces.

752
00:42:36,050 --> 00:42:38,860
Then we mix it with scallion-ginger water
and egg whites,

753
00:42:38,860 --> 00:42:40,880
salt, sugar, and other seasonings,

754
00:42:41,760 --> 00:42:44,630
knead it into fist-sized balls by hand,

755
00:42:45,440 --> 00:42:46,630
and simmer the meat balls in rich stock.

756
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:59,420
♪ Beneath coral branches,
delicacies abound ♪

757
00:42:47,110 --> 00:42:48,110
When simmering,

758
00:42:48,420 --> 00:42:49,550
we must keep the heat low

759
00:42:49,550 --> 00:42:50,940
and the cooking time long.

760
00:42:50,940 --> 00:42:53,030
Because the broth is thick

761
00:42:53,470 --> 00:42:54,920
and the color rich,

762
00:42:55,360 --> 00:42:56,440
ordinary folk also

763
00:42:56,730 --> 00:42:59,330
call this dish "Lion's Head."

764
00:43:03,760 --> 00:43:09,890
♪ Golden goblets shimmer like stars ♪
